=== Coagulation and Microclot Biomarkers
<subsec:coagulation-biomarkers>

Coagulation system dysregulation has emerged as an active area of ME/CFS biomarker research, driven primarily by Pretorius and colleagues' identification of fibrin amyloid microclots in Long COVID and ME/CFS. Nunes et al.\ (2022) reported hyperactivated platelets and fibrinaloid microclots in ME/CFS plasma from 25 patients and 15 controls, with microclot area commonly more than 10-fold greater than in healthy plasma, a mean platelet spreading score of 2.72 ± 1.24 against 1.00 in controls, and platelet hyperactivation confirmed by PAC-1 and CD62P surface staining @NunesPlatelets2022mecfs. Proteomics analysis further revealed dysregulation of the coagulation cascade, endothelial dysfunction markers, and complement machinery.

*A controlled count has not reproduced the abundance finding.* In 151 never-hospitalised participants with Long COVID and recovered controls, microaggregate number, microaggregate area and fibrin fibre density were all comparable across groups, and D-dimer, Clauss fibrinogen, von Willebrand factor antigen, soluble P-selectin and PAI-1 did not differ @Fraser2026LCcoagulation. That cohort has Long COVID rather than ME/CFS, and its discounted certainty is 0.51, so it constrains the Long COVID extension of this biomarker claim without refuting the ME/CFS measurement. It does mean the panel below is a research hypothesis rather than an established signature. The assay also has no external reference standard and was scored visually without blinding in several studies @Cochrane2023Plasmapheresis @lim:microclot-quantification-unvalidated.

Key candidate coagulation biomarkers:
    - *D-Dimer*: Elevated in a subset of ME/CFS patients; reflects fibrin degradation and microclot turnover
    - *PAI-1 (plasminogen activator inhibitor-1)*: Elevated PAI-1 impairs fibrinolysis, allowing microclot persistence in the microvasculature
    - *Von Willebrand Factor (VWF)*: Marker of endothelial activation; elevated in endothelial injury
    - *Fibrinogen*: Precursor to fibrin microclots; elevated levels support clot formation propensity
    - *Soluble P-Selectin*: Platelet and endothelial activation marker; elevated in ME/CFS in some studies


